Z||000000||BurlyGoat||09-06-2001||02:06 PM||||Hopefully someone will have a suggestion. The 86se V6 I recently purchased had been sitting for 3 or 4 years...Thus the brakes lines where in terrible shape. I decided to replace the brake lines, calipers, and pads (funny enough the rotors were pretty good). I have bought a line of 3/16 brake line for the back and front runs of line. I only have a flaring tool for standard flaring (not the bubble flaring that is used on the Fiero), so I bought adapters and all is well with these lines. Problem is the 1/4 (or what I think is a 1/4 line) trunk line. This line runs from the master cylinder to the rear passenger wheel (a T connector). I can't seem to find the proper brass fitting for the two ends. <P>Anyone have a suggestion on what I am looking for ?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
